meta {
  name: Learn an attachment into memory
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/attachments/{{attachmentId}}/learn?progress_token={{progressToken}}
}

docs {
  Promote a per-question chat attachment into **permanent** memory: the already-uploaded file
  is ingested into the rolling Uploads connector, so it becomes chunked, embedded, graphed and
  citable like any other document.

  Attaching a file is context for ONE question by design; this is the explicit opt-in that
  makes it memory. In the UI it is the "Learning permanently" toggle beside the staged files,
  and the agent can call it when you ask it to learn an attached document.

  The attachment itself is untouched and stays downloadable. 410 if the retention sweep has
  already deleted the bytes (re-attach it), 404 if the id is unknown.

  `progress_token` is optional — omit the query param entirely for the plain behaviour (what
  the CLI/agent's `qj_api` tool use). Pass one to make this request's real chunk-embedding
  progress readable via `Poll ingest progress` while it's still running.
}
